{"alignments":[],"candidates":[{"additionalConceptCount":3,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"6","reason":"△ACD ∼ △CBD, giving AD/CD = CD/BD. Thus CD² = AD × BD = 4 × 9 = 36, so CD = 6.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"cn-math","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"cnm_273_q3","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[]},{"additionalConceptCount":1,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B: 7√3","reason":"Similarity gives BD² = AD·DC = 12, so BD = 2√3. Thus the area is (1/2)(3 + 4)(2√3) = 7√3. Alternatively, AB² + BC² = (9 + BD²) + (16 + BD²) = 49 gives the same altitude.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2009_AMC_10A_Q10","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"id":"altitude-similarity","label":"Right-triangle altitude similarity","nodeIds":["cnm_273"]},{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_112","cnm_171","cnm_116","cnm_271","cnm_272"],"id":"solution:altitude-similarity:1fedba14d274","label":"Use similarity across the altitude","methodDirectNodeIds":{"altitude-similarity":["cnm_273","cnm_p148"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_273","cnm_p148","cnm_112","cnm_171","cnm_116","cnm_271","cnm_272"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":2,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D, 1:4","reason":"Put p=AC and q=CB. The shaded area is π[(p+q)²-p²-q²]/8 = πpq/4. Since CD²=((p+q)/2)²-((p-q)/2)²=pq, the comparison circle has area πpq. The ratio is therefore 1:4.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1967_AMC_12_Q33","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"id":"diameter-altitude-similarity","label":"Right-triangle altitude similarity","nodeIds":["cnm_254","cnm_273"]},{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_p192","cnm_055","cnm_148","cnm_271","cnm_272","cnm_116"],"id":"solution:diameter-altitude-similarity:712144b8bc73","label":"Use the altitude of a right triangle","methodDirectNodeIds":{"diameter-altitude-similarity":["cnm_p150","cnm_254